{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/554791-what-will-happen-to-1st-requiem-s-clan-books-since-2nd-version-is-out","id":554791,"title":"What will happen to 1st Requiem's Clan Books since 2nd version is out ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-14T13:47:14-07:00","id":554791,"title":"What will happen to 1st Requiem's Clan Books since 2nd version is out ?","content":"Hi guys,<br /> <br /> While waiting for the translation of the Requiem's 2nd version (to french), i am considering rewriting all my NPCs with the help of the five clan books, which are all reviewed as very good.<br /> My question is : are they going to be rewritten in the following of Blood and Smoke ? Are they compatible (background settings AND rule settings) with the 2nd version ?<br /> I am a bit in the dark here, as i didn't read neither the new corebook neither the clan books. I just do not want to spend a 100box here if I will have to buy new versions in the next years.<br /> <br /> Thanks !<br /> <br /> Edit : Actually the same questions goes for the 5 covenant books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6461,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","user":"essen_ko","date":". 06-14-2015, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","name":"essen_ko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:54:36-07:00","id":554819,"title":"","content":"All of the background and setting material from the Clan books is still valid and fully compatible with 2nd edition. They're even listed in the 2nd edition core book as recommended inspirational reading. The rules are still usable as well, but may require some minor house ruling to fit into the 2nd edition rules. But they are fairly easy to incorporate if you want to. There are not currently any plans to remake the Clan books for 2nd edition, so you definitely don't need to worry about having to buy new versions of the same book in a year or so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:55:50-07:00","id":554837,"title":"","content":"The clan books are compatible, that's called out in the Inspirational Media section in the Introduction chapter, along with Damnation City. The rules would likely have to be changed, but they're small parts of the clan books, mostly merits.<br /> <br /> The covenants have changed enough that they're putting out a Secrets of the Covenants book, but I've no idea when it will be out. Setting-wise, you wouldn't have to change much to fit first edition covenant stuff into second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:04:35-07:00","id":554852,"title":"","content":"Ok, thank you for the infos.<br /> I will then wait to read the convenants changes, and rush on the clans add-on !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","name":"essen_ko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:20:25-07:00","id":554971,"title":"","content":"Okay, then one more question :<br /> <br /> Does buying the Danse Macabre book still makes sense now that the new version is out ?<br /> Or is it the same content that is summarise in 2nd version ? Which would make sense, as Danse Macabre came out in 2012 as a support for all the new ideas.<br /> I've heard the Banes system; the new mask and vices and virtues; the new social &quot;fight&quot; system; the &quot;hunter like&quot; three way ladder system; all this is present and fully developed in blood and smoke (once again, i am waiting for the translation to get into the new version, kickstarter starts in about a week here in France, so please understand that i am about six months delayed here ! )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","name":"essen_ko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T17:05:42-07:00","id":555007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>essen_ko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/554791-what-will-happen-to-1st-requiem-s-clan-books-since-2nd-version-is-out?p=554971#post554971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, then one more question :<br /> <br /> Does buying the Danse Macabre book still makes sense now that the new version is out ?<br /> Or is it the same content that is summarise in 2nd version ? Which would make sense, as Danse Macabre came out in 2012 as a support for all the new ideas.<br /> I've heard the Banes system; the new mask and vices and virtues; the new social &quot;fight&quot; system; the &quot;hunter like&quot; three way ladder system; all this is present and fully developed in blood and smoke (once again, i am waiting for the translation to get into the new version, kickstarter starts in about a week here in France, so please understand that i am about six months delayed here ! )</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>Danse Macabre</i> has lots of hacks for the game, some of which (in modified forms) made it in Blood and Smoke. Not all of them - impossible, with many of them being exclusive. It's also got alternative covenants, with some basic rule stuff, chronicle seeds, a section on Gargoyles. If you want to ticker with the rules and setting, consider it. If not, well, it's probably less in your interests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:04:24-07:00","id":555077,"title":"","content":"I think Danse Macabre is still worth getting. True, a lot of the same ideas from Danse Macabre are also present in Second Edition, but with different execution. But it's still worth it if you are comfortable with using system hacks, because it presents similar ideas in different ways, as well as some completely different ideas, all of which come together to give you a lot to tinker with. If you're not into tinkering with the system you can pass on it, but if you like to homebrew, it's well worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:05:09-07:00","id":555078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>essen_ko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/554791-what-will-happen-to-1st-requiem-s-clan-books-since-2nd-version-is-out?p=554971#post554971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, then one more question :<br /> <br /> Does buying the Danse Macabre book still makes sense now that the new version is out ?</div> </div> </div> </div> Personally, I'm going to say it depends on what your'e trying to do. Danse Macabre came out at the same time as other Chronicler Guides were being made, but Requiem already had a book named that, so I think of it as a kind of Requiem Chronicler Guide 2. The big thing is that its a lot of hacks to the game - first, we should ask if you want to make a bunch of changes to the game?<br /> <br /> The first part of the book talks about how to make different &quot;tier&quot; games work - at the street (covenants become philosophies), city (default), and global level. If you're happy with just the city level stuff, there's no change; while I like this section, its very short. Later on, there's also some new covenants to chew over, if you want them; personally, I think they act a lot like just variations on existing covenants, and have used them to inspire factions within my existing covenants rather than use them as their own thing.<br /> <br /> The hacks to the clans are outdated, I think. Masks and Dirges likewise have turned into the new vampire virtue/vice already.<br /> <br /> Then, we start getting into system hacks. Now, I like the Edge from social combat in theory, but I've found that players tend to avoid the social combat parts; meanwhile, we've had a blast with social maneuvering. No one's ever been interested in &quot;Mental Combat,&quot; though I've had success with Discipline Combat, ripping off the Duel Arcane. Down and Dirty Combat? Tilts? Part of 2e by default. Dead Echoes: Manifesting Disciplines gives bonuses to synergetic skills. Which, while interesting in theory, is just flat bonuses to skills; kind of redundant with things like Vigor or Majesty already granting bonuses; given the boost in power of disciplines, you really don't need skill bonuses. Not quite outdated, but certainly not worthwhile in my opinion.Hell is Other People feels like the Touchstone mechanic. Banes are part of core rules now. Dearly Devoted gave some rules for making devotions (outdated with how the disciplines work now) and the idea you can get devotins from a quest instead of XP spending (don't need book for).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Atrocity still works if you want an alternative Humanity system to work with. Its completely different in theme and feel from both what the new Humanity reflects, but if you want to really play up the atrocious monster, this is for you. The Gargoyle stuff is still relevant.<br /> <br /> Last chapter of the book deals with some sample chronicle ideas, nothing really jumping out that isn't covered elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, in the end, Danse Macabre really only helps out with different tier games, suggested new covenants, some setting ideas, the Gargoyles, and maybe an alternative Integrity system if you like it really dark. Something between a seventh and a tenth of the entire book possibly relevant, and most of that depends on how much you like going through books like this for story ideas instead of making them on your own. If you prefer doing your own stories, or have other sources, then that just leaves Gargoyles, which isn't enough of a draw to buy the book.<br /> <br /> I personally do not suggest the book - I'd recommend Damnation City first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-14-2015, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T06:55:26-07:00","id":555590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/554791-what-will-happen-to-1st-requiem-s-clan-books-since-2nd-version-is-out?p=554837#post554837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The clan books are compatible, that's called out in the Inspirational Media section in the Introduction chapter, along with Damnation City. The rules would likely have to be changed, but they're small parts of the clan books, mostly merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact most of the merits from the clanbooks get already updated versions in Blood &amp; Smoke, so no problem there. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/35536-of-rose-and-thorn-pack-minded-and-other-savage-systems-or-not\">This</a> topic touches on a little of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T03:14:44-07:00","id":556719,"title":"","content":"Apparently Convenants books are now pretty much outdatted. (most of them came out in 2005/06 !)<br /> and clan books are still valid.<br /> <br /> Damnation City is hell of a read, whoa !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","name":"essen_ko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T07:53:12-07:00","id":556883,"title":"","content":"The Covenant books can be great inspiration, but I wouldn't use them straight up, since they go into a level of detail that is often contradictory with the theme or literal background of the 2E Covenants.<br /> <br /> So while I might use the Lancea Sanctum book for ideas on the rites Sanctified perform, I definitely don't use it just straight up, because some of its components are outdated. The Ordo book is probably the best example of this: Tons of great stuff in there, but a change in how the Ordo was formed in 2e makes the info presented there about Dracula and his Wives feel a bit ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:43:04-07:00","id":557012,"title":"","content":"Personally, I suggest just avoiding the Covenant books altogether, even if for inspiration. Too many things are different, and making the changes to the 2e version is hard enough without the old baggage. With it, its annoyingly difficult to not fall into traps. YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}